  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">GCRF:Thanzi la Onse (Health of All):  Frameworks and analysis to ensure value for money health care - developing theory, changing practice</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Global Challenges Research Fund (GCRF) supports cutting-edge research to address challenges faced by developing countries. The fund addresses the UN sustainable development goals. It aims to maximise the impact of research and innovation to improve lives and opportunity in the developing world.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UKRI GROW award - Thanzi la Onse, which means &#x2018;Health of All&#x2019; in a Malawian language, will construct a model of Malawi&#x2019;s entire health system, and then test various interventions within it. The model will map not just the health of Malawians but also the country&#x2019;s resources and how the health system operates. This activity benefits Malawi and Uganda.</narrative>
  </description>
